# Project Atlas — non-negotiable rules

1. TRADING_MODE defaults to "paper". Never change this default.
2. Live order submission must always require: LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=true,
   KILL_SWITCH_ENABLED=false, valid exchange credentials, risk engine
   healthy, market data healthy, database healthy, reconciliation healthy,
   and a valid manual live-approval token — ALL simultaneously. Never
   remove or weaken any of these checks, even temporarily, even for testing.
3. Every order must pass through app/risk/engine.py. No execution code may
   call an exchange or the paper engine directly, bypassing risk checks.
4. Use Decimal for all price/quantity/balance/fee/P&L values. Never float.
5. All timestamps are UTC.
6. Never hardcode or print API keys/secrets. Use app/core/security.py's
   redact() helpers before logging anything that touches Settings.
7. The AI analysis layer (app/ai/) is advisory only — it must never call
   order-submission code directly, and its output must be labeled advisory
   in the API response and UI.
8. Every rejected trade must be persisted with a reason code, not just
   approved trades.
9. Read docs/architecture/roadmap.md before starting any phase. Do not
   start a phase whose prerequisites aren't marked done.
10. Write tests alongside every module you create, not after. Target 90%+
    coverage on app/risk/ and app/execution/ specifically.
